# --- M6 / N17 -------------------------------------------------------------
# `tools/`, `pokelike/data/*` and `docs/reference` were all ignored WHOLESALE,
# with no negation pattern and zero tracked files beneath them. Three separate
# audits flagged the consequences, and they were not cosmetic:
#
#   * `tools/battle-oracle/compare.py` has been a standing acceptance gate in
#     every milestone since M3. None of it survived a clean clone.
#   * `tools/extract-data/` regenerates files under `pokelike/data/` -- and
#     BOTH were ignored, so neither the outputs nor the thing that rebuilds
#     them was in the repository.
#   * `pokelike/data/` is not derived and not optional: it is the ported game
#     data (pokedex, moves, type chart, item pools, trainer and submap
#     tables). `import pokelike` does not work without it. R2 flagged
#     `node_presentation.json` specifically.
#   * `docs/reference/` holds the CODEX audit that every renderer-track brief
#     cites as its authority. Prose; nothing regenerates it.
#
# The policy now matches `route-oracle/`'s (see its block below): track
# everything, ignore ONLY genuinely derived artifacts, and pin a hash so
# nothing required is invisible.
#
# Deliberately still ignored, because each is regenerable from tracked inputs:
#   * `tools/battle-oracle/out/` -- a 3.2 MB executable slice of the (tracked)
#     bundle. `tools/battle-oracle/prefix.sha256` pins its expected hash and
#     `compare.py` now REGENERATES it when absent and verifies that hash on
#     every run, so a clean clone runs the gate rather than failing on it.
#   * `tools/extract-data/out/` -- the intermediate extraction tables, rebuilt
#     from the tracked bundle by the tracked scripts beside them.
#   * `tools/extract-data/node_modules/` (already covered by the global rule).
tools/battle-oracle/out/
tools/extract-data/out/

# route-oracle: everything is tracked EXCEPT three regenerable artifacts.
#   * `out/` -- the derived JS prefix, a 3.4 MB slice of the (tracked) bundle.
#     `route-oracle/prefix.sha256` pins its expected hash and `compare.py`
#     re-extracts and verifies it on every run, so nothing required is
#     invisible -- see route-oracle/README.md.
#   * `findings/streams/` -- deterministically regenerable via `compare.py --dump`.
#   * `node_modules/` (already covered by the global rule below) -- installed
#     from the TRACKED `route-oracle/package.json` + `package-lock.json` with
#     `npm --prefix route-oracle ci`. Only `scan-toplevel-danger.js` needs it.
route-oracle/out/
route-oracle/findings/streams/


